# LIQUID-06 — Avoid cache-breaking date operations

## Rationale

Passing `'now'` to the `date` filter returns the current timestamp, which changes
every second. That makes rendered output differ on each request, breaks Shopify's
page cache, and hurts performance. Prefer pre-calculated values, metafields
maintained by Shopify Flow, or client-side time logic.

## How to check

```bash
bun "<skill-dir>/scripts/cli.ts" check liquid-performance <file>
```

Flags `'now' | date` and similar cache-breaking date comparisons.

## How to fix

Move time-sensitive comparisons to JavaScript, use Flow/automation for time-based
badges, or serialize a static timestamp once without comparing to `now` in Liquid.

## Examples

### Bad

```liquid
{% if product.metafields.custom.drop_date != blank %}
  {% assign available = product.metafields.custom.drop_date | date: '%s' %}
  {% assign now = 'now' | date: '%s' %}
  {% if now > available %}
    {% assign days = now | minus: available | divided_by: 86400.00 %}
    {% if days < settings.new_badge_days %}
      {% assign showNewBadge = true %}
    {% endif %}
  {% endif %}
{% endif %}
```

### Good

```liquid
{% if product.metafields.custom.drop_date != blank %}
  {% assign drop_date_timestamp = product.metafields.custom.drop_date | date: '%s' %}
  <div data-drop-date="{{ drop_date_timestamp }}" class="product-availability">
    <!-- Handle time-based logic with JavaScript -->
  </div>
{% endif %}
```
